{"name":"Temperate Taupe","hex":"#bfb1aa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"temperate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Moderate; not excessive.","Specifically, moderate in temperature."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To render temperate; to moderate"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temperate"},{"term":"taupe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-grey colour, the colour of moleskin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taupe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Temperate climate","blocks":[{"text":"In geography, the temperate climates of Earth occur in the middle latitudes, which span between the tropics and the polar regions of Earth. These zones generally have wider temperature ranges throughout the year and more distinct seasonal changes compared to tropical climates, where such variations are often small; they usually differ only in the amount of precipitation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Koppen-Geiger_Map_v2_C_1991%E2%80%932020.svg/330px-Koppen-Geiger_Map_v2_C_1991%E2%80%932020.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temperate_climate","wikidata":"Q167466"},{"title":"Taupe","blocks":[{"text":"Taupe is a dark gray-brown color. The word derives from the French noun taupe meaning \"mole\". The name originally referred only to the average color of the French mole, but beginning in the 1940s, its usage expanded to encompass a wider range of shades."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taupe","wikidata":"Q2307593"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Latitude_zones.png/500px-Latitude_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Latitude_zones.png/1280px-Latitude_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Latitude_zones.png/500px-Latitude_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The different geographical zones of the world. The temperate zones, in the sense of geographical regions defined by latitude, span from either north or south of the tropics (north or south of the red strip) to the polar circles.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALatitude_zones.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Talpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg/500px-Talpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Talpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg/1280px-Talpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Talpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg/500px-Talpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A mole","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATalpa_europaea_MHNT.jpg"}],"sounds":{"temperate":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/En-us-temperate.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6c/En-us-temperate.ogg/En-us-temperate.ogg.mp3"}],"taupe":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/En-us-taupe.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5b/En-us-taupe.ogg/En-us-taupe.ogg.mp3"}]}}}